# Without a type: the only caller hands over a number or undefined. One comparison of the bits tells them apart: a number is stored as it is, and undefined becomes the one NaN, a constant.
# CHECK-LABEL: name="put" role=Source
# CHECK: Int64 b@[[bits]] = BitwiseCast(b@[[value]], {{*}}:TypeTest)
# CHECK: Int32 b@[[isNumber]] = LessThan(b@[[bits]], {{*}}:TypeTest)
# CHECK: Branch(b@[[isNumber]], Terminal, {{*}}:TypeTest)
# CHECK: Store(b@[[value]], b@{{*}}, ControlDependent|Writes:TypedArrayElements, {{*}}:PutTypedArrayElement)
# CHECK: Store({{*}}, b@{{*}}, ControlDependent|Writes:TypedArrayElements, {{*}}:PutTypedArrayElement)
# CHECK-LABEL: end of function
# Nothing is boxed, and nothing is stored by key.
# NONE-LABEL: name="put" role=Source
# NONE-NOT: :ElemSet)
# NONE-NOT: Select(
# NONE-LABEL: end of function
# CALLS: f1: size=
# CALLS-NOT: stub
# CALLS: operation operationAOTTypedArrayPut x2
# CALLS-NOT: stub
# CALLS: f{{*}}: size=
# Both arms call for a view whose length may change, so those moves follow the calling convention.
# X64: instructions: 17, patchpoints: 2, rare instructions: 9
# ARM64: instructions: 20, patchpoints: 2, rare instructions: 10
